Subject: [PATCH] rockchip: fit: let the OTA routing env pick the boot_fit partition

The transactional OTA routing env (uboot-env-prefill.sh / fwenv.sh,
"KEEP IN SYNC" trio) points boot_fit at the raw boot partition for
normal boot and at the PARTLABEL=recovery partition for rescue via
"setenv boot_fit_part <name>". The 2017.09 vendor tree honours that
variable; the v5 (v2025.04) fit_get_blob() only selects between
PART_BOOT and PART_RECOVERY from plat_boot_mode(), so the rescue fit
branch could never find its partition. Read the override from the
environment and fall back to the boot-mode based selection.

Staged for legacy/u-boot-rockchip-v5 builds only
(uboot-rescue-default-env.sh); the distro-form trees keep the
boot-mode based selection.
---
--- a/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/fit.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/fit.c
@@ -151,8 +151,15 @@
 	char *part_name = PART_BOOT;
 	void *fit, *fdt;
 	int blk_num;
+	const char *boot_fit_part;
 
-	if (plat_boot_mode() == BOOT_MODE_RECOVERY) {
+	/* Seeed OTA routing: the transactional env points boot_fit at the raw
+	 * boot or PARTLABEL=recovery partition explicitly; keep the boot-mode
+	 * based selection as the fallback when the override is unset. */
+	boot_fit_part = env_get("boot_fit_part");
+	if (boot_fit_part && *boot_fit_part) {
+		part_name = (char *)boot_fit_part;
+	} else if (plat_boot_mode() == BOOT_MODE_RECOVERY) {
 		if (!ab_is_enabled() || ab_can_find_recovery_part())
 			part_name = PART_RECOVERY;
 	}
